utating operation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and mutation operations can’t be performed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a concurrent execution context like a child task."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Refer to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" documentation for detailed discussion of semantics shared between all task groups."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Discarding-behavior","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Discarding behavior"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A discarding task group eagerly discards and releases its child tasks as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"soon as they complete. This allows for the efficient releasing of memory used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by those tasks, which are not retained for future "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" calls, as would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be the case with a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Cancellation-behavior","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Cancellation behavior"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A discarding task group becomes canceled in one of the following ways:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"when "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/cancelAll()"},{"type":"text","text":" is invoked on it,"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"when the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task"},{"type":"text","text":" running this task group is canceled."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscardingTaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" is a structured concurrency primitive, cancellation is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"automatically propagated through all of its child-tasks (and their child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tasks)."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A canceled task group can still keep adding tasks, however they will start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"being immediately canceled, and may act accordingly to this. To avoid adding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new tasks to an already canceled task group, use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/addTaskUnlessCancelled(priority:operation:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than the plain "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/addTask(priority:operation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" which adds tasks unconditionally."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For information about the language-level concurrency model that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscardingTaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" is part of,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],"t